<article class="env-lemma" id="08UN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08UN">Lemma <span data-tag="08UN">92.8.7</span>.</a> Let $A \to B$ be a local ring homomorphism of local rings. Let $A^ h \to B^ h$, resp. $A^{sh} \to B^{sh}$ be the induced maps of henselizations, resp. strict henselizations. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  L_{B^ h/A^ h} = L_{B^ h/A} = L_{B/A} \otimes _ B^\mathbf {L} B^ h \quad \text{resp.}\quad L_{B^{sh}/A^{sh}} = L_{B^{sh}/A} = L_{B/A} \otimes _ B^\mathbf {L} B^{sh}  \]
</div>
  <p> in $D(B^ h)$, resp. $D(B^{sh})$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The complexes $L_{A^ h/A}$, $L_{A^{sh}/A}$, $L_{B^ h/B}$, and $L_{B^{sh}/B}$ are all zero by Lemma <a href="/tag/08R2" data-tag="08R2">92.8.4</a>. Using the fundamental distinguished triangle (<a href="/tag/08QS" data-tag="08QS">92.7.0.1</a>) for $A \to B \to B^ h$ we obtain $L_{B^ h/A} = L_{B/A} \otimes _ B^\mathbf {L} B^ h$. Using the fundamental triangle for $A \to A^ h \to B^ h$ we obtain $L_{B^ h/A^ h} = L_{B^ h/A}$. Similarly for strict henselizations. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>